---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, ''); // "" or "/partner-scrape"

// Sprint 010, ticket 002 (issue 16): terse, link-dense landing page for
// an LLM/agent that followed `llms.txt` (ticket 004) -- or reached this
// URL directly. States the exact data URLs so the page is self-sufficient
// without `llms.txt`; defers the full schema to `/data-access` (Design
// Rationale D2 -- never duplicate the field table) and points partner-
// side agents at `/publish-events`.
//
// Origin used for the absolute data URLs below: `DATA_ORIGIN` is derived
// from `import.meta.env.SITE` (the build-time `site:`, which a `--site`
// CLI flag overrides at config-merge time) plus `base`, rather than a
// hardcoded literal. This page tree is now built for several origins from
// one codebase -- production Pages, the beta's build-time checkout under
// `/partner-scrape`, and the Docker beta -- and deriving the origin means
// there is nothing to keep in sync across them.
//
// Do NOT hardcode `https://www.sdstemecosystem.org` here. Verified live,
// not assumed:
//
//   $ curl -sI https://www.sdstemecosystem.org/          -> 200, but the
//     body is a 417-byte HTML4 `<frameset>` whose only `<frame>` points
//     at https://league-infrastructure.github.io/partner-scrape/ -- it
//     is not the site itself, so a plain HTTP client (an agent, not a
//     frame-rendering browser) that GETs that domain never reaches real
//     content.
//   $ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' \
//       https://www.sdstemecosystem.org/data/partners.json     -> 404
//   $ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' \
//       https://league-infrastructure.github.io/partner-scrape/ -> 200
//
// That frameset is a registrar/DNS-level misconfiguration (neither repo
// has a Pages custom domain configured) tracked separately from this
// codebase. Until it is fixed, the www domain resolves to a frame, so a
// build that stamps it into these URLs would print URLs that 404 for any
// plain HTTP client.
//
// Sprint 017, ticket 002 (issue 42): step 3 below adds `teams.json` --
// a structurally independent dataset from the partners/events pair
// above (own self-describing `meta` envelope, no reconstruction
// relationship to steps 1-2). Per this page's own Design Rationale D2
// ("never duplicate the field table"), the full `Team` field list
// stays on `/data-access` only; this page states just the fetch URL
// and one-line envelope shape, same as it already does for steps 1-2.
const DATA_ORIGIN = `${import.meta.env.SITE.replace(/\/+$/, '')}${base}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="For Agents | SD STEM Ecosystem"
  description="Machine-readable data behind the San Diego STEM Ecosystem: exact data URLs, the reconstruction contract, and where to publish events."
>
  <section class="hero hero-sm">
    <h1>For Agents</h1>
    <p>Structured JSON behind the San Diego STEM Ecosystem opportunity directory. No auth, no API key, no rate limit imposed by us.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="agents-page container">
    <section class="agents-section">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        A directory of STEM learning opportunities (camps, out-of-school programs, work-based
        learning) run by San Diego-area partner organizations. Two file kinds, statically served,
        plain JSON: a partner roster and, per partner, a current-events file and a past-events
        file. <code>partners.json</code> plus every referenced partner's event files fully
        reconstruct the opportunity data on this site — no other source needed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="agents-section">
      <h2>Data</h2>
      <p>Fetch in this order:</p>
      <pre class="code-block"><code>{`1. GET ${DATA_ORIGIN}/data/partners.json
   -> { generated_at, partner_count, partners: [...] }
   Each partner has a "slug", "events_url", "past_events_url"
   (both paths relative to .../data/).

2. For each partner, GET:
   ${DATA_ORIGIN}/data/partners/<slug>/events.json
   ${DATA_ORIGIN}/data/partners/<slug>/past-events.json
   -> { generated_at, partner_slug, kind, event_count, events: [...] }
   "current"/"past" is a true partition -- undated records land in
   past-events.json, nothing is dropped.

3. GET ${DATA_ORIGIN}/data/teams.json
   -> { meta: { generated, total, by_league, by_location_precision,
   out_of_region }, teams: [...] }
   Independent of steps 1-2 -- the FIRST/VEX robotics teams directory
   for San Diego County, self-describing via its own meta envelope.`}</code></pre>
      <p>
        That's the full URL surface — no other endpoint exists. Field-by-field definitions for
        every partner, event, and team property, plus a worked example of each file shape, are on
        <a href={`${base}/data-access`}>How to Consume Our Data</a>; this page does not repeat
        them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="agents-section">
      <h2>Links</h2>
      <ul class="agents-links">
        <li><a href={`${base}/data-access`}>/data-access</a> — full schema, envelope shape, reconstruction contract, worked example.</li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/publish-events`}>/publish-events</a> — acting on a partner's behalf and want their events ingested? Publishing methods, ordered easiest-first.</li>
        <li><a href={`${base}/opportunities`}>/opportunities</a> — this same data, rendered for a human.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-sm {
    min-height: auto;
    padding: 100px 20px 40px;
  }

  .agents-page {
    padding: 40px 15px 60px;
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .agents-section {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .agents-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .agents-section p {
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .agents-section code {
    font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--purple-faint);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--dark);
  }

  .agents-links {
    line-height: 1.9;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .code-block {
    background: var(--dark-deep);
    color: var(--white);
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .code-block code {
    font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
    white-space: pre;
  }
</style>
